README refs
     1	# dev-loops
     2	
     3	Turn a GitHub issue into a merged PR autonomously, up to a human-approval checkpoint.
     4	
     5	**Harness-agnostic by design.** The same dev loop runs three ways over one shared core (`packages/core`): as a **Claude Code plugin**, as a **Pi extension**, and as a standalone **CLI**. Routing, gates, and phases are defined once in the core; the plugin and extension are thin integrations over that shared workflow.
     6	
     7	## What is a dev loop?
     8	
     9	A dev loop takes a GitHub issue through seven lifecycle phases — from intake to merge — with deterministic routing, self-correcting review gates, and autonomous execution until a human approves. The phase is always consultable from the deterministic state model in `packages/core/src/loop/lifecycle-state.mjs`.
    10	
    11	| Phase | What happens |
    12	|---|---|
    13	| `issue_intake` | Normalize the issue, confirm scope, detect linked PRs |
    14	| `refinement` | Elaborate the spec, run a bounded audit, harden acceptance criteria |
    15	| `implementation` | Build the accepted scope on a feature branch or via Copilot |
    16	| `draft_gate` | Gate review at the draft→ready boundary before marking the PR ready |
    17	| `feedback_resolution` | Fix, reply to, and resolve review threads on GitHub |
    18	| `pre_approval_gate` | Final gate review: verify evidence, CI, and unresolved threads |
    19	| `merge` | Merge the PR and write the retrospective checkpoint |
    20	
    21	The public routing contract is the [Public Dev Loop Contract](./skills/docs/public-dev-loop-contract.md).
    22	
    23	## Quick start
    24	
    25	`dev-loop` is the single public entrypoint. Drive it in natural language — it resolves the authoritative current state, picks the correct internal strategy, and routes deterministically. You never name internal strategies.
    26	
    27	```text
    28	start dev loop on issue 112       # start work on an issue
    29	auto dev loop on issue 112        # run autonomously to the human-approval checkpoint
    30	continue dev loop on PR 88        # continue follow-up on an open PR
    31	```
    32	
    33	See the canonical shorthand mapping in the [Public Dev Loop Contract](./skills/docs/public-dev-loop-contract.md).
    34	
    35	## Commands
   120	
   121	```bash
   122	npx dev-loops@<version> gates   # print what reviewers will check
   123	```
   124	
   125	Key surfaces:
   126	
   127	- **Gate angles** — which review lenses run at the draft and pre-approval gates
   128	- **Personas** — focused per-angle prompts (DRY, KISS, YAGNI, SRP, SoC, and more)
   129	- **Refinement** — fan-out count and mode for parallel review variants; `refinement.maxCopilotRounds` caps Copilot re-review rounds (default `5`). Set `maxCopilotRounds: 0` to disable the Copilot gate entirely — local-harness-only review (`draft_gate → pre_approval_gate`), useful when the repo has no Copilot reviewer configured.
   130	- **Autonomy** — which gates require operator confirmation
   131	- **Workflow defaults** — retrospective enforcement, draft-first posture, dev-mode policy
   132	
   133	Full details: [Extension Documentation](./extension/README.md) and `packages/core/src/config/extension-defaults.yaml`.
   134	
   135	## Docker
   136	
   137	A deterministic container image with all required tooling for dev-loop operation.
   138	
   139	```bash
   140	docker build -t dev-loops .
   174	# Full dev-loop over a live repo worktree mounted at /workspace
